# InterGenOS pkm — repo cache directories, created at every boot.
#
# PI-218-1 (.218 post-install eval, 2026-06-27): a non-root READ command —
# InterGen's manage_packages dispatch, or `pkm search` / `list-available` —
# on a FRESH install crashed FileNotFoundError on /var/cache/pkm/db because
# the directory did not exist yet. pkm-check-updates.service's
# CacheDirectory=pkm only creates /var/cache/pkm when that timer-service
# runs, and pkm/repo.py:_ensure_cache_dirs cannot create it as a non-root
# reader (root owns /var/cache). systemd-tmpfiles creates it on every boot,
# as root, before anything reads it — closing the pre-first-sync window.
#
# Modes mirror pkm/repo.py:_ensure_cache_dirs: packages/ is 0700 (L-021 —
# block a non-root local user staging an attacker archive between the
# SHA256-verify and the tar-extract); db/ is world-readable so a non-root
# search can read the (root-written, signed) synced index.
d /var/cache/pkm          0755 root root -
d /var/cache/pkm/db       0755 root root -
d /var/cache/pkm/packages 0700 root root -

# The mutation lock file, created at every boot.
#
# pkm serializes its operations on an flock over this path. A WRITER creates it
# if it is missing, because a writer runs as root. A READER cannot: since the
# read commands began taking a SHARED lock here, an unprivileged `pkm list` or
# `pkm verify` needs a file it can open, and /var/lock resolves to /run/lock,
# which is root-owned 0755 and emptied at every boot. Nothing the reader does
# can bring the file into existence there, so the package ships it and
# systemd-tmpfiles recreates it after each boot — the same reason the cache
# directories above are declared here rather than created on first use.
#
# 0644: every user on the machine may read their own system's package state,
# so every user must be able to open this file. The flock is advisory and the
# file holds nothing; write access is not needed to take a shared lock, and
# granting it would let any local user block pkm by taking the lock
# exclusively.
f /var/lock/pkm.lock      0644 root root -
